  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2018) position from NRB Commercial Bank's own audited annual report multi-year key-financial table, taken from the FY2018 report (the reporting year's own document). Basis note: the FY2015-FY2019 summary tables are CONSOLIDATED — the FY2018 report's 67,142.86 for FY2018 is its consolidated balance-sheet total, against 67,061.86 solo, a 0.12% difference — while the FY2020 and later tables are SOLO. The gap is immaterial in size but the basis genuinely changes at FY2020 and should be treated as a break when comparing across it. Off-balance-sheet trap: the FY2022 report's summary table prints FY2018 total assets as 86,598.12, which is that year's balance-sheet total (67,142.86) plus its off-balance-sheet items (19,455.25) — the sum is exact. Its FY2019 and later columns exclude off-balance-sheet items. This dataset never sources FY2018 total assets from that report. The FY2021 report is excluded entirely: its only extractable table is a horizontal analysis in which every value is a percentage of a base year, so it carries no usable figures at all. Calculated line item(s): total_capital. total_capital, where derived, is this report's own Tier-I plus Tier-II rather than a later report's total, so the capital stack stays internally consistent. car_pct, where derived, is total capital over risk-weighted assets. classified_loans, where derived, is the reported ratio applied to reported loans and advances. GAP-FILL -- the FY2018 report does not print 4 row(s), taken from the nearest report that does: investments_securities from AR2022, tax_expense from AR2022, classified_loans from AR2020, provision_classified from AR2020. Total assets are never gap-filled, to keep the off-balance-sheet-inflated columns out of the series. RESTATEMENTS -- 5 figure(s) here differ in other NRBC reports; the contemporaneous value is kept: reserve_fund: this record uses 1061.29 (AR2018); AR2019 report 1050.34; operating_profit: this record uses 1904.16 (AR2018); AR2019 report 1889.26; tier1_capital: this record uses 6825.53 (AR2018); AR2022 report 6778.83; tier2_capital: this record uses 578.83 (AR2018); AR2022 report 573.68; capital_surplus_deficit: this record uses 1162.24 (AR2018); AR2019 report 1130.82.",
